To implement the domino chain logic, I need to replace the placeholder `formChain` method with a backtracking algorithm that attempts to build a valid chain.

I will:
1. Add necessary imports (`ArrayList`, `Iterator`).
2. Implement `formChain` to handle edge cases (empty list, single domino).
3. Implement a recursive helper `findChain` that tries to append unused dominoes to the current chain, handling orientation flips.
4. Ensure the final check verifies the chain is closed (first and last numbers match).

Here is the updated `Dominoes.java`:

Dominoes.java
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Iterator;
import java.util.List;

class Dominoes {

    List<Domino> formChain(List<Domino> inputDominoes) throws ChainNotFoundException {
        if (inputDominoes == null || inputDominoes.isEmpty()) {
            return new ArrayList<>();
        }

        List<Domino> remaining = new ArrayList<>(inputDominoes);
        List<Domino> chain = new ArrayList<>();

        // Start with the first domino
        chain.add(remaining.remove(0));

        if (findChain(chain, remaining)) {
            return chain;
        } else {
            throw new ChainNotFoundException("No chain found");
        }
    }

    private boolean findChain(List<Domino> chain, List<Domino> remaining) {
        if (remaining.isEmpty()) {
            // Check if the chain is closed: first left == last right
            if (chain.isEmpty()) {
                return true;
            }
            Domino first = chain.get(0);
            Domino last = chain.get(chain.size() - 1);
            return first.getLeft() == last.getRight();
        }

        Iterator<Domino> iterator = remaining.iterator();
        while (iterator.hasNext()) {
            Domino domino = iterator.next();
            iterator.remove();

            // Try orientation 1: left matches previous right
            if (chain.isEmpty() || chain.get(chain.size() - 1).getRight() == domino.getLeft()) {
                chain.add(domino);
                if (findChain(chain, remaining)) {
                    return true;
                }
                chain.remove(chain.size() - 1);
            }

            // Try orientation 2: right matches previous left (flip)
            if (chain.isEmpty() || chain.get(chain.size() - 1).getRight() == domino.getRight()) {
                chain.add(new Domino(domino.getRight(), domino.getLeft()));
                if (findChain(chain, remaining)) {
                    return true;
                }
                chain.remove(chain.size() - 1);
            }

            // Restore the domino to remaining list for other branches
            remaining.add(domino);
        }

        return false;
    }

}
```
